  "body": "## What changed\n\nA two-setup document posted as one program ran from Setup 1's last cut straight into Setup 2's first, on a part still clamped for Setup 1. A new document post option, **Between setups**, decides what posts at a setup change:\n\n| Word | Label | Posts |\n|---|---|---|\n| `pause` (default) | Pause (M0) | a program stop after each setup's last operation, with a comment naming the next setup |\n| `optional-stop` | Optional stop (M1) | the same, as an optional stop |\n| `continue` | Run straight on | the old program |\n| `file-per-setup` | One file per setup | one whole program per setup (the multi-file post) |\n\n- `crates/app/src/posting_setup_change.rs` (new): folds the stop into the setup's last operation's after-action, so each dialect writes it where it writes an operator's own stop (spindle and coolant off), and adds `PARAM SetupChange \"<next setup>\"` for the comment. Independent of \"Skip pauses and homes\" (a proven program still needs the part turned over). A Go home at the change is refused by name; an operation's own M0 there merges into the one stop. Per mount (one file: one machine, and one post unless an explicit script posts them all): a mount's last operation gets no stop, so two setups on different posts still post one clean file each.\n- `assets/posts/fanuc.cps`: at a setup-change stop, `G91 G28 Z0`, `G90`, `(SETUP CHANGE - NEXT: <setup>)`, then M0/M1.\n- `assets/posts/tormach.cps`: now declares `afterModes` (it never read stops before, so a stop on Tormach was refused); writes `G53 G0 Z..`, `(MSG, SETUP CHANGE - NEXT: <setup>)`, M0/M1; a Go home is refused there (the G30 spot is the operator's preset).\n- `crates/post/src/post/engine.rs`: a script without `afterModes` is refused at a setup change by name (once, not doubled by the generic after-operation refusal).\n- One file per setup splits the mounts per setup (`post_mounts`); the one-file post refuses such a program by name.\n- Project key `post_options.between_setups` (only written off default; an unknown word refuses to open); setup-owned post options carry it and are compared for it by the program-level check.\n- UI: a \"Between setups\" combo box under the post options, through `SetPostOptions`.\n- MCP: `post` takes an optional `between_setups` word, applied first through the undoable `SetPostOptions` (or `SetSetupPostOptions` when the active setup owns its options); the camcraft-mcp skill row says so.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1532-setup-boundary-stop.md`.\n\nProcess change: yes (the camcraft-mcp skill's `post` row).\n\n## Goldens changed\n\n- `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/tormach/live_then_stop.refusal`: the \"does not declare afterModes\" warning is gone, because tormach.cps now reads after-actions (3 warnings instead of 4; the program is still refused).\n\nNo NC golden changed.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests, `crates/app/tests/between_setups.rs`:\n- `the_default_pauses_between_setups_on_fanuc_with_a_comment_naming_the_next`\n- `the_default_pauses_between_setups_on_tormach_and_an_optional_stop_writes_m1`\n- `run_straight_on_is_the_old_program_and_is_undoable`\n- `one_file_per_setup_writes_two_whole_programs`\n- `a_post_that_cannot_stop_is_refused_by_name_at_the_setup_change`\n- `a_go_home_at_the_setup_change_is_refused_by_name`\n- `the_choice_round_trips_and_the_default_writes_no_key`\n- `the_mcp_post_tool_takes_the_choice_through_the_undoable_command`\n\nUpdated: `setup_post_options::a_setup_that_skips_posts_without_its_stops_while_the_other_follows_the_document` (now sets Run straight on, since its two setups would otherwise pause between them).\n- `program_entry::pause_and_home_entries_post_goldens_and_tormach_refuses_by_name`: Tormach now reads after-actions, so its Go home refusal is tormach.cps's own (\"a trip home is asked after the operation in operation <name> ...\") instead of the engine's afterModes refusal.\n- `setup_mount::two_setups_on_different_posts_post_one_file_each` unchanged; it caught the first cut of the fold placing the stop per machine (fixed in the second commit).\n\nQuick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`): green on head 6d171bf07 (post ok 35s, app ok 914s, ui ok 64s; logs gate-logs/quick-20261114-091458). The previous run, on 51c1611f9, failed program_entry and setup_mount; both are fixed in the second commit. Clippy on camcraft-app, camcraft-post, camcraft-ui: clean (`-D warnings`).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real control ran the output: the Fanuc and PathPilot programs are checked by text only.\n- The other afterModes dialects (Haas, Mazak, Sinumerik, Heidenhain, ...) write the stop without the Z lift and the comment: follow-up #1647.\n- The UI combo box was not clicked in the running app (not launched).\n- The script `post` verb takes no between_setups argument (MCP and UI do).\n\nChangelog: A program that runs from one setup into the next now stops there by default (M0 with a comment naming the next setup); \"Between setups\" in the post options chooses an optional stop, running straight on, or one file per setup (#1532, PR #1650)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1532\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
